{"animath":"0.1","title":"E-Math trigonometry: ratios and the sine rule","level":"secondary","subject":"math","topic":"e-trigonometry","kind":"concept","canvas":{"width":960,"height":540},"scenes":[{"id":"s1","caption":"Meet the 3-4-5 triangle","narration":"A right-angled triangle with short sides 3 and 4. The sine of angle theta is opposite over hypotenuse: 3 over 5, or 0.6.","duration_ms":8000,"steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legOpp","kind":"line","x1":300,"y1":220,"x2":300,"y2":340,"stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"explain":"The opposite side: length 3, across from angle theta."}},{"at_ms":200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legAdj","kind":"line","x1":300,"y1":340,"x2":460,"y2":340,"stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"explain":"The adjacent side: length 4, next to angle theta."}},{"at_ms":400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"hyp","kind":"line","x1":300,"y1":220,"x2":460,"y2":340,"stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"explain":"The hypotenuse: length 5, the longest side."}},{"at_ms":600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"ra","kind":"rect","x":300,"y":316,"w":24,"h":24,"fill":"none","stroke":"#1a1a1a","strokeWidth":2,"explain":"The right-angle marker: 90 degrees."}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"probe","kind":"circle","cx":300,"cy":220,"r":9,"fill":"#1f7a3a","explain":"The tracing dot: it walks the three sides so you can name each one."}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"move","target":"probe","to":{"cx":300,"cy":340},"dur_ms":1000},{"at_ms":2000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labOpp","kind":"text","x":120,"y":290,"size":26,"text":"opposite = 3","explain":"Opposite = 3: the side across from theta."}},{"at_ms":2300,"do":"move","target":"probe","to":{"cx":460,"cy":340},"dur_ms":1000},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labAdj","kind":"text","x":355,"y":382,"size":26,"text":"adjacent = 4","explain":"Adjacent = 4: the side beside theta."}},{"at_ms":3700,"do":"move","target":"probe","to":{"cx":300,"cy":220},"dur_ms":1000},{"at_ms":4800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labHyp","kind":"text","x":425,"y":258,"size":26,"text":"hyp = 5","explain":"Hyp = 5: the longest side."}},{"at_ms":5100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"arcTick","kind":"line","x1":460,"y1":340,"x2":430,"y2":340,"stroke":"#b00020","width":3,"explain":"The angle arc: it marks angle theta."}},{"at_ms":5300,"do":"move","target":"arcTick","to":{"x2":436,"y2":322},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"angTheta","kind":"text","x":408,"y":296,"size":30,"text":"θ","explain":"Theta: the angle the ratios are measured from."}},{"at_ms":6500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"sinEq","kind":"latex","x":620,"y":120,"size":40,"color":"#1f7a3a","tex":"\\sin\\theta = \\frac{3}{5} = 0.6","explain":"sin theta = 3/5 = 0.6: opposite over hypotenuse."}},{"at_ms":6700,"do":"move","target":"sinEq","to":{"y":180},"dur_ms":500},{"at_ms":7400,"do":"hide","target":"probe"}]},{"id":"s2","caption":"Cosine and tangent join the card","narration":"Cosine of theta is adjacent over hypotenuse: 4 over 5. Tangent is opposite over adjacent: 3 over 4 - read the card as SOH CAH TOA.","duration_ms":9000,"steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legOpp","kind":"line","x1":300,"y1":220,"x2":300,"y2":340,"stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"explain":"The opposite side: length 3, across from angle theta."}},{"at_ms":100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"legAdj","kind":"line","x1":300,"y1":340,"x2":460,"y2":340,"stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"explain":"The adjacent side: length 4, next to angle theta."}},{"at_ms":200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"hyp","kind":"line","x1":300,"y1":220,"x2":460,"y2":340,"stroke":"#1a1a1a","width":4,"explain":"The hypotenuse: length 5, the longest side."}},{"at_ms":800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"cosEq","kind":"latex","x":600,"y":150,"size":40,"color":"#1f7a3a","tex":"\\cos\\theta = \\frac{4}{5} = 0.8","explain":"cos theta = 4/5 = 0.8: adjacent over hypotenuse."}},{"at_ms":1000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"dot4","kind":"circle","cx":380,"cy":340,"r":10,"fill":"#1f7a3a","explain":"A unit mark on the adjacent side: counting to 4."}},{"at_ms":1100,"do":"move","target":"dot4","to":{"cx":560,"cy":150},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":2000,"do":"hide","target":"dot4"},{"at_ms":2100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"dot5","kind":"circle","cx":380,"cy":280,"r":10,"fill":"#1f7a3a","explain":"A unit mark on the hypotenuse: counting to 5."}},{"at_ms":2200,"do":"move","target":"dot5","to":{"cx":640,"cy":150},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":3100,"do":"hide","target":"dot5"},{"at_ms":3200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tanEq","kind":"latex","x":600,"y":260,"size":40,"color":"#1f7a3a","tex":"\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4} = 0.75","explain":"tan theta = 3/4 = 0.75: opposite over adjacent."}},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"dot3","kind":"circle","cx":300,"cy":280,"r":10,"fill":"#1f7a3a","explain":"A unit mark on the opposite side: counting to 3."}},{"at_ms":3500,"do":"move","target":"dot3","to":{"cx":560,"cy":260},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":4400,"do":"hide","target":"dot3"},{"at_ms":4500,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"dot4b","kind":"circle","cx":380,"cy":340,"r":10,"fill":"#1f7a3a","explain":"A unit mark on the adjacent side: counting to 4."}},{"at_ms":4600,"do":"move","target":"dot4b","to":{"cx":640,"cy":260},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":5500,"do":"hide","target":"dot4b"},{"at_ms":5600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"soh","kind":"text","x":600,"y":360,"size":26,"text":"SOH: sin = opp/hyp","explain":"SOH: sine is opposite over hypotenuse."}},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"cah","kind":"text","x":600,"y":400,"size":26,"text":"CAH: cos = adj/hyp","explain":"CAH: cosine is adjacent over hypotenuse."}},{"at_ms":6800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"toa","kind":"text","x":600,"y":440,"size":26,"text":"TOA: tan = opp/adj","explain":"TOA: tangent is opposite over adjacent."}},{"at_ms":8100,"do":"emphasize","target":"tanEq","dur_ms":800}]},{"id":"s3","caption":"The sine rule for any triangle","narration":"Not every triangle has a right angle. The sine rule links each side with the sine of its opposite angle - here b works out to about 6.93.","duration_ms":9500,"steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"tri","kind":"polygon","points":[[250,380],[550,380],[430,180]],"fill":"none","stroke":"#1a1a1a","strokeWidth":4,"explain":"The triangle: angles A = 30 degrees and B = 60 degrees, side a = 4 known."}},{"at_ms":800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labA","kind":"text","x":268,"y":348,"size":28,"text":"A = 30°","explain":"Angle A: 30 degrees."}},{"at_ms":1600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labB","kind":"text","x":494,"y":348,"size":28,"text":"B = 60°","explain":"Angle B: 60 degrees."}},{"at_ms":2400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labSideA","kind":"text","x":502,"y":272,"size":28,"text":"a = 4","explain":"Side a: length 4, opposite angle A."}},{"at_ms":3200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labSideB","kind":"text","x":296,"y":272,"size":28,"text":"b = ?","explain":"Side b: unknown, opposite angle B - what we solve for."}},{"at_ms":3400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"alt","kind":"line","x1":430,"y1":180,"x2":430,"y2":230,"stroke":"#1f7a3a","width":3,"explain":"The shared altitude h: it links the two halves of the triangle."}},{"at_ms":3500,"do":"move","target":"alt","to":{"y2":380},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":4400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labH","kind":"text","x":438,"y":408,"size":24,"text":"h: shared altitude","explain":"h: the altitude shared by both halves."}},{"at_ms":4800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"sineRule","kind":"latex","x":640,"y":180,"size":44,"color":"#1f7a3a","tex":"\\frac{a}{\\sin A} = \\frac{b}{\\sin B}","explain":"The sine rule: a over sin A equals b over sin B."}},{"at_ms":5000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"dotA","kind":"circle","cx":510,"cy":232,"r":10,"fill":"#1f7a3a","explain":"A substitution marker: it shows where a = 4 enters the rule."}},{"at_ms":5100,"do":"move","target":"dotA","to":{"cx":610,"cy":180},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":6000,"do":"hide","target":"dotA"},{"at_ms":6200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"subEq","kind":"latex","x":640,"y":290,"size":40,"tex":"\\frac{4}{\\sin 30^\\circ} = \\frac{b}{\\sin 60^\\circ}","explain":"Substituting: 4 over sin 30 degrees equals b over sin 60 degrees."}},{"at_ms":7000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"solveEq","kind":"latex","x":640,"y":400,"size":40,"color":"#1f7a3a","tex":"b = \\frac{4 \\times 0.8660}{0.5} \\approx 6.93","explain":"Solved: b = (4 times 0.8660) over 0.5, about 6.93."}},{"at_ms":7200,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"dotB","kind":"circle","cx":600,"cy":368,"r":10,"fill":"#1f7a3a","explain":"A substitution marker: it shows where the solved value lands."}},{"at_ms":7300,"do":"move","target":"dotB","to":{"cx":300,"cy":272},"dur_ms":900},{"at_ms":8300,"do":"hide","target":"dotB"},{"at_ms":8300,"do":"hide","target":"labSideB"},{"at_ms":8400,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"labSideB2","kind":"text","x":296,"y":272,"size":28,"text":"b ≈ 6.93","color":"#1f7a3a","explain":"b is about 6.93: the solved side length."}},{"at_ms":8600,"do":"emphasize","target":"sineRule","dur_ms":600}]},{"id":"s4","caption":"A common mistake: do not flip tangent","narration":"A tempting slip: writing tangent as adjacent over opposite. Opposite and adjacent swap places under pressure. Always read TOA: tan is opposite over adjacent.","duration_ms":7500,"steps":[{"at_ms":0,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"wrongEq","kind":"latex","x":300,"y":200,"size":44,"color":"#b00020","tex":"\\tan\\theta = \\frac{4}{3}","explain":"The wrong ratio: tan theta = 4/3, adjacent over opposite."}},{"at_ms":700,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"ghostBar","kind":"rect","x":150,"y":420,"w":60,"h":10,"fill":"#b00020","explain":"The ghost bar: height 1.33, taller than the whole unit square."}},{"at_ms":900,"do":"move","target":"ghostBar","to":{"y":270,"h":160},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":1800,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"ghostLab","kind":"text","x":60,"y":470,"size":24,"text":"4/3 = 1.33: taller than the whole","explain":"4/3 = 1.33: taller than the whole, so it must be wrong."}},{"at_ms":2600,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"rightEq","kind":"latex","x":620,"y":200,"size":44,"color":"#1f7a3a","tex":"\\tan\\theta = \\frac{3}{4}","explain":"The right ratio: tan theta = 3/4, opposite over adjacent."}},{"at_ms":3000,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"goodBar","kind":"rect","x":620,"y":420,"w":60,"h":10,"fill":"#1f7a3a","explain":"The correct bar: height 0.75, a proper part of the whole."}},{"at_ms":3200,"do":"move","target":"goodBar","to":{"y":340,"h":90},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":4100,"do":"show","shape":{"id":"goodLab","kind":"text","x":560,"y":470,"size":24,"text":"3/4 = 0.75: TOA, opp over adj","explain":"3/4 = 0.75: read TOA - opposite over adjacent."}},{"at_ms":4800,"do":"move","target":"wrongEq","to":{"y":60},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":4800,"do":"move","target":"ghostBar","to":{"y":420,"h":10},"dur_ms":800},{"at_ms":5700,"do":"hide","target":"ghostLab"},{"at_ms":6000,"do":"emphasize","target":"rightEq","dur_ms":800}]}]}